  "file": "narration.mp3",
  "transcript": "Here's the quickest way to see which remote jobs you can actually apply for. On Yari Careers there's a box right at the top. It says where do you live? Tap it in or pick worldwide roles only and the board shows the jobs that say they're open to you. Every card tells you where it hires from, when it was posted and the pay if the employer stated it. Tap the apply button and you're on the original posting. No account, nothing to pay. Links in the bio.",
